5 "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $f(x),g(x)\\in A,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f+g)(1) & =f(1)+g(1)\\le 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $A$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $f(x)\\in A$ and $k=-1\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & \\le 0 \\\\ kf(1) & \\ge k\\cdot 0 \\\\ (kf) & \\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $A$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $A$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\"" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294335 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294336 13194139534549 true] [17592186294335 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294337 13194139534549 true] [17592186294335 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294338 13194139534549 true] [17592186294335 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294339 13194139534549 true] [17592186294335 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294340 13194139534549 true] [17592186294335 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534549 true] [17592186294335 1041 "selection" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294335 1104 #edb/ref 17592186294336 13194139534549 true] [17592186294335 1110 #uuid "506d02c0-5619-5a27-a023-c555e254176f" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294336 1034 "I and IV only" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294336 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534549 true] [17592186294336 1111 #uuid "5481ebe6-7afc-5959-b9ff-3ac4af78b201" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294337 1034 "II and IV only" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294337 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534549 true] [17592186294337 1111 #uuid "30ebfb58-3bc7-569d-95bf-f02e3b8ca8a5" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294338 1034 "I only" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294338 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534549 true] [17592186294338 1111 #uuid "5d7679e4-a83a-5caf-a580-1ef94cc88f1a" 131941395