3194139534549 true] [17592186294416 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534549 true] [17592186294416 1111 #uuid "ce5c09b4-4d46-5559-b9ec-ec713538fe22" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294417 1034 "{2,4,8,12}" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294417 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534549 true] [17592186294417 1111 #uuid "722c1b51-99fc-5a0f-9c45-026ba6f2e0ff" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294418 1034 "{4,8,12}" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294418 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534549 true] [17592186294418 1111 #uuid "064cf5f7-3c6f-5a67-8ace-d0b029af5d6e" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294419 1034 "{4,8,10,12}" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294419 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534549 true] [17592186294419 1111 #uuid "d6964215-98b3-59b2-9c5f-b58ada618e90" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294420 1017 #edb/ref 17592186294421 13194139534549 true] [17592186294420 1089 "q-91157" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294420 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534549 true] [17592186294420 1100 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -13 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294420 1113 #uuid "bc8df3f8-8c99-53c4-bedf-bdbc4a64bd8d" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294420 1145 "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above ${a}_{33}=-2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -13 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}.$" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294421 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294422 13194139534549 true] [17592186294421 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294423 13194139534549 true] [17592186294421 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294424 13194139534549 true] [17592186294421 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294425 13194139534549 true] [17592186294421 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294426 13194139534549 true] [17592186294421 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534549 true] [17592186294421 1041 "selection" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294421 1104 #edb/ref 17592186294423 13194139534549 true] [17592186294421 1110 #uuid "91453757-9831-5a7f-a75f-008cfb4d956e" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294422 1034 "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{3}$" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294422 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534549 true] [17592186294422 1111 #uuid "a1a7de62-7a35-54d1-8c8d-37d7f5614485" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294423 1034 "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}$" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294423 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534549 true] [17592186294423 1111 #uuid "f43e5710-c564-555a-9a7f-521cd35962f5" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294424 1034 "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{3}$" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294424 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534549 true] [17592186294424 1111 #uuid "f504898f-1440-5d44-84d4-545d39402603" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294425 1034 "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}$" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294425 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534549 true] [17592186294425 1111 #uuid "998c5e56-9f8c-5bc2-96d7-f5db11fcaabb" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294426 1034 "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}$" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294426 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534549 true] [17592186294426 1111 #uuid "a1e7a766-c691-56f0-aed9-b86ed86706a2" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294427 1017 #edb/ref 17592186294428 13194139534549 true] [17592186294427 1089 "q-99815" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294427 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534549 true] [17592186294427 1100 "Consider the following set of functions:\n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(t)=t,\\,{f}_{2}(t)={t}^{2},\\,{f}_{3}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space $C[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ of continuous functions over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨f(t),g(t)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(t)g(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n- ${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n- $S={{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{3}(t)}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product\n\n*Hint: $⟨{f}_{2},{f}_{3}⟩=0.$*" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294427 1113 #uuid "2b2b13a3-b44a-55c4-8d9d-88dc0a7ddd0d" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294427 1145 "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is called orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩ & =⟨t,{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }t\\cdot {t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{4}}{4}{|}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{4}}{4}-(\\frac{(-\\pi )^{4}}{4}) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that ${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{3}(t)⟩=⟨t,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's use integration by parts. We denote\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=t & ⟹ & {u}^{′}=1, \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & ⟹ & v=\\int {v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, applying the integration by parts formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =uv{|}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{u}^{′}v\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t){|}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(-\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-(-(-\\pi )\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )))+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{|}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\pi +\\pi +(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )) \\\\  & =2\\pi \\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that ${f}_{1}(t)⊥̸{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since ${f}_{1}(t)⊥̸{f}_{3}(t),$ the set $S$ is *not* orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294428 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294429 13194139534549 true] [17592186294428 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294430 13194139534549 true] [17592186294428 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294431 13194139534549 true] [17592186294428 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294432 13194139534549 true] [17592186294428 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294433 13194139534549 true] [17592186294428 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534549 true] [17592186294428 1041 "selection" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294428 1104 #edb/ref 17592186294432 13194139534549 true] [17592186294428 1110 #uuid "625d4615-372e-5bdf-afa5-48dbb67b8a87" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294429 1034 "None of the statements are true" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294429 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534549 true] [17592186294429 1111 #uuid "12cc649e-b5f5-533c-9ef4-e499f926f551" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294430 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534549 true] [17592186294430 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 1319